# Regenerated by capture.mjs before every design pass. Committing them would freeze a
# design review against a build nobody is running any more, which is the exact failure
# the capture script exists to prevent.
screens/
web/

# A 534 MB snapshot of real TMDB, re-taken with `npm run design:snapshot`, and the
# screenshots it produces — the same convention as `screens/` above. §6.151.
real/
real-screens/

# The web's real pass, same convention — and it was committed by mistake in §6.157's
# close-out, 38 files and 6.3 MB, because this list was written before the directory
# existed and `git add -A` does not know what a convention is. §6.158.
web-real/

# Photographs taken to make one finding checkable — a before and an after of one screen
# — rather than a pass over every route. Same convention as the four above and for the
# same reason: an image committed here is an image somebody will still be reading after
# the build it is of has gone. The finding names the file and its hash.
#
# The **probe** beside them is not ignored, and that is the point of naming the pattern
# rather than the directory: a number nobody can re-derive is a number nobody can check,
# so the script that produced the measurement is committed and the pictures are not.
found/*.png
